From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luisyr <106528106+luisyr1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro-komodo: Describe
 the AoC

Enable Trusty, the GSA, the AoC's three mailboxes and the AoC itself
with komodo's stock board config (dtbo fragment 104: "KM4", id
0x40802, rev 0x10000; fragment 121: GNSS type 2) and its sensor rails
(fragment 7: LDO7S and LDO5S of the S2MPG15), as zumapro-tegu does.

The firmware is the owner's vendor/firmware/aoc.bin under the name
aoc-komodo.bin; it is never shipped. The AoC is not started by this
change: Trusty, the GSA and the AoC drivers are modules, blacklisted on
komodo, that a start script loads in order before it writes the
firmware name to the AoC's sysfs node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts | 57 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 57 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
index 153917b..2c55f33 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
@@ -283,6 +283,63 @@
 			};
 		};
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The AoC's sensor rails, stock dtbo fragment 7 (sensor_1v8 = LDO7S
+	 * "L7S_SENSORS", sensor_3v3 = LDO5S "L5S_PROX"), as on tegu.
+	 */
+	pmic-2 {
+		compatible = "samsung,s2mpg15-pmic";
+
+		regulators {
+			komodo_sensor_3v3: ldo5s {
+				regulator-name = "sensor-3v3";
+			};
+
+			komodo_sensor_1v8: ldo7s {
+				regulator-name = "sensor-1v8";
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * The AoC (Always-on Compute), the audio and sensor DSP. Its firmware is
+ * the owner's own signed vendor/firmware/aoc.bin, installed as
+ * aoc-komodo.bin and authenticated by the GSA; Trusty's hwmgr.aoc starts
+ * it. Board config "KM4", id 0x40802, rev 0x10000 and GNSS type 2 are
+ * stock dtbo fragments 104 and 121. Nothing here starts the AoC: its
+ * drivers are modules that only the start script loads, in order.
+ */
+&aoc {
+	memory-region = <&aoc_reserved>;
+	firmware-name = "aoc-komodo.bin";
+	google,board-id = <0x40802>;
+	google,board-rev = <0x10000>;
+	google,gnss-type = <2>;
+	sensor-1v8-supply = <&komodo_sensor_1v8>;
+	sensor-3v3-supply = <&komodo_sensor_3v3>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aoc_mbox_a32 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aoc_mbox_f1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aoc_mbox_p6 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&gsa {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&trusty {
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &ap2apm_mailbox {
